1
00:00:25,852 --> 00:00:43,219
[SPEAKER_00]: In terms of speech, right speech and wrong speech, speech that we should abstain from, and speech that we should actually cultivate.

2
00:00:44,719 --> 00:00:49,561
[SPEAKER_00]: So, there's this... the main... the main... the obvious one is lying.

3
00:00:50,481 --> 00:00:51,702
[SPEAKER_00]: This is vusavada.

4
00:00:53,382 --> 00:01:02,188
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, obviously, you know, the precepts and then the precepts around the speech, they just needs to be... they need to be taken as standards.

5
00:01:02,248 --> 00:01:03,449
[SPEAKER_00]: So, say you are able

6
00:01:24,143 --> 00:01:51,499
[SPEAKER_01]: To abstain from it, and you don't compromise that standard, even if... even if your life... even if you have to experience more nuisance and hassle and hardship on account of you not telling lies, it's still good to not tell lies and sustain that standard, because it's... well, then, that will enable you, then, to start seeing the problem of speech on a subtler level.

7
00:01:54,160 --> 00:02:08,687
[SPEAKER_01]: Because, you know, each time you speak, each time you communicate with others for an unenlightened mind, there are already these implications of ownership, self-view, me, others, internally, externally, communication, company.

8
00:02:08,827 --> 00:02:11,169
[SPEAKER_01]: All of that is maintained and sustained through speech.

9
00:02:12,589 --> 00:02:19,833
[SPEAKER_01]: That's why people often, when they try to, like, even just sort of minimize their speech, you start feeling this pressure.

10
00:02:21,022 --> 00:02:28,348
[SPEAKER_01]: You don't have to just speak or say something or chat or communicate, because existence is maintained through your communication.

11
00:02:28,409 --> 00:02:30,911
[SPEAKER_01]: But none of that would be really...

12
00:02:32,078 --> 00:02:37,280
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not seen correctly or benefited from, unless you can even keep the basic precepts concerning the speech.

13
00:02:37,500 --> 00:02:44,404
[SPEAKER_01]: So, no lying, no malicious tail-bearing, spreading of gossip.

14
00:02:44,504 --> 00:02:45,844
[SPEAKER_01]: You have to abstain from that.

15
00:02:46,445 --> 00:02:53,688
[SPEAKER_01]: But then, yes, then you also get to see that, and often many suttas, like when the Buddha was addressing monks as well, not just lay people,

16
00:02:54,188 --> 00:02:57,470
[SPEAKER_01]: It was about don't, you know, don't be engaging in frivolous speech.

17
00:02:57,550 --> 00:02:59,191
[SPEAKER_01]: Speech that's pointless.

18
00:02:59,411 --> 00:03:01,132
[SPEAKER_01]: Which is the point of speech?

19
00:03:01,152 --> 00:03:03,913
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, any speech that has nothing to do with the dhamma, it's pointless speech.

20
00:03:05,554 --> 00:03:12,457
[SPEAKER_01]: And it should at least make a person think, because it sounds like, oh, wow, so I can't speak at all.

21
00:03:12,917 --> 00:03:16,859
[SPEAKER_01]: And it's like, but why is that a problem?

22
00:03:16,899 --> 00:03:19,861
[SPEAKER_01]: Why is it a problem to be silent?

23
00:03:22,112 --> 00:03:24,172
[SPEAKER_01]: If there is a need for something to be said, sure.

24
00:03:24,933 --> 00:03:33,474
[SPEAKER_01]: But why do you also feel this pressure to say something in company, that it has no practical value, and yet you can't help it and you have to say it?

25
00:03:34,635 --> 00:03:36,255
[SPEAKER_00]: I was like, well, that is a problem, actually.

26
00:03:37,215 --> 00:03:39,856
[SPEAKER_01]: Psychologically, that is a problem for a mind that wants to develop.

27
00:03:41,896 --> 00:03:48,517
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's exactly the point of solitude and abstaining from pointless, frivolous speech, unless it's connected with the dhamma or some practical purpose.

28
00:03:49,258 --> 00:03:50,418
[SPEAKER_01]: You get to see that, that

29
00:03:51,518 --> 00:04:03,247
[SPEAKER_01]: Oh, yeah, there's this dependence on this pressure to speak, to communicate, to say something, to touch the world on that level, so to speak, to keep in touch with it, so everything is fine.

30
00:04:03,808 --> 00:04:10,913
[SPEAKER_01]: And often, there is that kind of slightly anxious... Oh, just, you know, just touch base, just keep it, just...

31
00:04:11,274 --> 00:04:11,914
[SPEAKER_01]: Okay, it's all good.

32
00:04:11,934 --> 00:04:12,395
[SPEAKER_01]: Are you good?

33
00:04:12,435 --> 00:04:12,995
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah, yeah, okay.

34
00:04:13,736 --> 00:04:13,916
[SPEAKER_01]: No.

35
00:04:14,196 --> 00:04:15,557
[SPEAKER_01]: It's your idea that's all good.

36
00:04:15,597 --> 00:04:16,798
[SPEAKER_01]: That's what you're trying to protect.

37
00:04:17,799 --> 00:04:19,940
[SPEAKER_01]: And it's all... it's a form of control.

38
00:04:20,911 --> 00:04:23,233
[SPEAKER_01]: It's a form of like, okay, so it's fine, so then I'm fine.

39
00:04:23,953 --> 00:04:26,355
[SPEAKER_01]: But the fact that you need to do that means it's not fine.

40
00:04:27,375 --> 00:04:35,421
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's what probably the first thing a person that withdraws into solitude and stops speaking gonna feel is that insecurity and anxiety from not communicating and speaking.

41
00:04:36,061 --> 00:04:37,282
[SPEAKER_01]: But you have to go through that.

42
00:04:38,903 --> 00:04:41,045
[SPEAKER_01]: And then when you do speak, you speak with a purpose.

43
00:04:43,146 --> 00:04:49,951
[SPEAKER_01]: And you certainly don't speak out of that pressure to just speak something, to say something, you know, because I'm a bit awkward or, you know,

44
00:04:50,768 --> 00:04:51,969
[SPEAKER_01]: You know, is everything okay?

45
00:04:51,989 --> 00:04:52,850
[SPEAKER_01]: Is everything not okay?

46
00:04:53,251 --> 00:04:59,997
[SPEAKER_01]: So, all of those are your doubts, your own hindrances, and here you are acting out of it, because speech is a form of action.

47
00:05:00,017 --> 00:05:00,997
[SPEAKER_00]: And it needs to be restrained.

48
00:05:01,678 --> 00:05:05,641
[SPEAKER_01]: You need to stop, as we often say, you need to stop acting out of unwholesome states.

49
00:05:06,202 --> 00:05:11,026
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, doubt, insecurity, awkwardness, all of that, acting out of that is unwholesome.

50
00:05:11,807 --> 00:05:12,648
[SPEAKER_01]: Not immoral,

51
00:05:13,605 --> 00:05:17,546
[SPEAKER_01]: But we're not talking about now, as I said, basic precepts that make you moral or immoral.

52
00:05:17,686 --> 00:05:18,607
[SPEAKER_01]: That has to be covered.

53
00:05:18,627 --> 00:05:20,668
[SPEAKER_01]: You have to be a moral person keeping the virtue.

54
00:05:21,428 --> 00:05:34,332
[SPEAKER_01]: Now, if you want to be the contemplative that does develop its own mind on account of, you know, solitude, correct reflection, gradual training that we often speak about, eh... yeah, you realize speech is a form of action.

55
00:05:34,453 --> 00:05:36,533
[SPEAKER_01]: And I keep acting out of compulsion almost.

56
00:05:38,094 --> 00:05:39,194
[SPEAKER_00]: So, I need to restrain that.

57
00:05:40,175 --> 00:05:40,935
[SPEAKER_01]: I need to endure it.

58
00:05:41,897 --> 00:05:46,559
[SPEAKER_01]: And certainly not act when I know for sure it's rooted in unwholesome.

59
00:05:49,961 --> 00:05:53,363
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, not necessarily anger or something, but yeah, like just frivolous.

60
00:05:53,523 --> 00:05:55,804
[SPEAKER_01]: It's unwholesome from the point of view of mind development.

61
00:05:55,864 --> 00:05:58,205
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you could just reflect for yourself.

62
00:05:58,486 --> 00:06:00,246
[SPEAKER_01]: So, why can't I just be silent?

63
00:06:01,667 --> 00:06:05,729
[SPEAKER_01]: Endure this pressure and say something when something needs to be said.

64
00:06:06,210 --> 00:06:06,790
[SPEAKER_01]: But otherwise,

65
00:06:08,078 --> 00:06:09,479
[SPEAKER_01]: Don't compromise that criteria.

66
00:06:10,399 --> 00:06:20,404
[SPEAKER_01]: And, you know, that's that's how the Buddha encouraged even the monks that had to kind of group and stay in a group and live together for one practical reason or the other at a time to just be silent.

67
00:06:21,924 --> 00:06:26,446
[SPEAKER_01]: Not like you take this blind sense of duty vow of silence.

68
00:06:26,746 --> 00:06:27,567
[SPEAKER_01]: I will never speak.

69
00:06:27,647 --> 00:06:30,268
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, now it's just you assume another external observance.

70
00:06:31,473 --> 00:06:32,173
[SPEAKER_01]: No.

71
00:06:32,273 --> 00:06:34,194
[SPEAKER_01]: You could speak for the right reason.

72
00:06:34,614 --> 00:06:35,094
[SPEAKER_01]: That's true.

73
00:06:35,134 --> 00:06:36,574
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not like, I can...

74
00:06:36,654 --> 00:06:37,815
[SPEAKER_01]: I'll just never act again.

75
00:06:38,175 --> 00:06:45,337
[SPEAKER_01]: That's the equivalent of taking up this, I'll never speak, I'll never do any of this, I'll never, you know, I'll never act again.

76
00:06:45,537 --> 00:06:46,457
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, that's your action.

77
00:06:47,938 --> 00:06:56,020
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you cannot act, but you can certainly unlearn to act out of pressure, to act out of unwholesome states.

78
00:06:59,685 --> 00:07:07,328
[SPEAKER_01]: Because it's a very, very much a physical thing, speech, that you act out.

79
00:07:08,508 --> 00:07:15,451
[SPEAKER_00]: But if you can't actually be aware of the speech, then there is no awareness of your mind.

80
00:07:15,491 --> 00:07:16,291
[SPEAKER_00]: Exactly.

81
00:07:16,351 --> 00:07:18,352
[SPEAKER_01]: So that's only the precepts, the behavior.

82
00:07:19,112 --> 00:07:20,252
[SPEAKER_01]: That's fine, you know.

83
00:07:20,272 --> 00:07:21,513
[SPEAKER_01]: You have to be restrained.

84
00:07:21,533 --> 00:07:22,293
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not really like...

85
00:07:24,741 --> 00:07:27,783
[SPEAKER_01]: I mean, a lot can be said about it, but there is really no need to.

86
00:07:27,883 --> 00:07:28,423
[SPEAKER_01]: It's obvious.

87
00:07:28,863 --> 00:07:30,784
[SPEAKER_01]: You have to just do it.

88
00:07:30,804 --> 00:07:34,826
[SPEAKER_01]: With any sort of virtue must be developed beforehand in terms of physical behavior and action.

89
00:07:35,527 --> 00:07:45,692
[SPEAKER_01]: But then it comes to speech, and often even the Buddha himself would, you know, the common eight precepts, and then he would just have those four or five different types of speech that are included in the basic precepts.

90
00:07:46,540 --> 00:07:52,081
[SPEAKER_01]: Because you realize that is like a kind of a practical point of converging for a mind that does want to develop.

91
00:07:52,521 --> 00:08:12,865
[SPEAKER_01]: Sure, you're abstained from, you know, physical immorality by body, with your actions, but there is now a lot that's sort of still coming through your speech, even not in a coarse manner, still keeps you basically connected to that physical... well, the assumptions in regard to the physical world you've been acting out of.

92
00:08:14,694 --> 00:08:20,097
[SPEAKER_01]: So, if you can't... if you cannot develop and sustain perspective in regard to your own speech, abstain from it.

93
00:08:20,737 --> 00:08:25,939
[SPEAKER_01]: Practice, as we said in some old talks, you know, like a... like develop the sense of a non-speaking mouth.

94
00:08:26,620 --> 00:08:35,104
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, literally, you are aware that you could speak, but you are not speaking and you haven't been speaking for a while, unless there was a purpose.

95
00:08:35,564 --> 00:08:37,965
[SPEAKER_01]: That becomes now an upgrade of your virtue.

96
00:08:38,795 --> 00:08:47,244
[SPEAKER_01]: In the same sense, the Buddha would speak about keeping the sense of physical restraint, guarding the sense doors, creates this aggregate of virtue.

97
00:08:47,664 --> 00:08:54,811
[SPEAKER_01]: So, basically, certain behavior you haven't been engaging for a while, because you've been keeping the precepts, becomes this solid thing that's now seen.

98
00:08:56,593 --> 00:08:57,774
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not like you're doing it.

99
00:08:58,255 --> 00:08:59,616
[SPEAKER_01]: It's what you haven't been doing.

100
00:09:00,395 --> 00:09:05,841
[SPEAKER_01]: For a while, the mind recognizes, oh, I've been dwelling in the state of not doing these things.

101
00:09:06,261 --> 00:09:11,927
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's when that joy, when a kind of unbroken virtue arises, that would encourage you should think about.

102
00:09:12,407 --> 00:09:19,915
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, in the same sense, you then get to see your own non-speaking mouth, that only been speaking when there was a purpose, no more spilling.

103
00:09:21,142 --> 00:09:36,590
[SPEAKER_01]: Through this physical orifice that you are communicating with the world, you were, no more spilling for pointless purpose, for sensual purpose, for angry purpose, and you become aware of the fact that, yes, the power of speech has been harnessed, so to speak.

104
00:09:36,930 --> 00:09:39,131
[SPEAKER_01]: You are not spilling out into the world carelessly.

105
00:09:39,471 --> 00:09:46,895
[SPEAKER_01]: You're not perverting the order and maintaining your assumptions of sensuality and anger and everything else through non-speaking mouth, mouth that hasn't been speaking.

106
00:09:49,413 --> 00:09:57,379
[SPEAKER_01]: So, the certain standard of when it's being spoken becomes now your criteria on account of which a samādhi and sense of joy can arise.

107
00:09:58,620 --> 00:10:02,203
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, what's happening in your mind becomes even more clearer.

108
00:10:02,783 --> 00:10:09,749
[SPEAKER_01]: And then, you could exactly, as the Guru would say himself, once you start developing the sense of samādhi towards jhāna, it's like the mind becomes pliable.

109
00:10:10,509 --> 00:10:11,570
[SPEAKER_01]: If you want to think this, you think that.

110
00:10:11,590 --> 00:10:12,751
[SPEAKER_01]: If you don't, you don't think it.

111
00:10:12,791 --> 00:10:13,392
[SPEAKER_01]: Mind listens.

112
00:10:14,213 --> 00:10:21,317
[SPEAKER_01]: Because you stop spilling it, and perverting it, and perturbing it, through physical and verbal careless actions, out of pressure, and so on.

113
00:10:21,337 --> 00:10:22,758
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it's a very practical thing.

114
00:10:22,818 --> 00:10:28,801
[SPEAKER_01]: It's not like, hey, abstain from your speech, just for some holy reason that will become apparent later on.

115
00:10:29,081 --> 00:10:42,469
[SPEAKER_01]: It's an actual training of a whole independent domain of action, through which you've been maintaining your wrong views, and so, and everything else, that basically keeps you liable to dukkha and non-control of your own mind.

116
00:10:44,108 --> 00:10:47,270
[SPEAKER_01]: So, it might feel like a bit sort of oppressive in the beginning.

117
00:10:47,330 --> 00:10:48,271
[SPEAKER_01]: I can't speak, I can't speak.

118
00:10:48,311 --> 00:10:50,513
[SPEAKER_01]: But, again, you take it on.

119
00:10:50,533 --> 00:11:01,421
[SPEAKER_01]: In the same sense, you take the behavior of the precepts, and then it becomes apparent, like, I am dwelling in a kind of... in a mode of being of non-speech.

120
00:11:02,361 --> 00:11:04,423
[SPEAKER_01]: Non-speaking mouth is my presence.

121
00:11:04,503 --> 00:11:05,263
[SPEAKER_01]: It's my reality.

122
00:11:05,604 --> 00:11:09,486
[SPEAKER_01]: My mouth that hasn't been speaking on account of greed, aversion, delusion.

123
00:11:09,607 --> 00:11:10,968
[SPEAKER_01]: Same, like, aggregate of virtue,

124
00:11:11,912 --> 00:11:14,053
[SPEAKER_01]: It gets upgraded into aggregative silence.

125
00:11:15,473 --> 00:11:16,473
[SPEAKER_01]: Unless there is a purpose.

126
00:11:16,493 --> 00:11:23,196
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you're not artificially or externally adhering to, I must be silent to not compromise the value of silence.

127
00:11:23,296 --> 00:11:23,436
[SPEAKER_01]: No.

128
00:11:24,096 --> 00:11:34,079
[SPEAKER_01]: All I need to do is not abandon the gateway where unwholesome things will become a reason for me breaking the silence, and silence remains unperturbed, even when I speak.

129
00:11:36,387 --> 00:11:44,410
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's why after the first jhāna, the second jhāna is called the Noble Silence, when you quiet even your thoughts, on account of already quieting your speech.

130
00:11:45,091 --> 00:11:47,652
[SPEAKER_01]: And by the way, that's another maybe side thing.

131
00:11:47,972 --> 00:11:53,854
[SPEAKER_01]: People think, like in the first jhāna, you quiet your thoughts, and that's why your speech kind of falls off, the vāti-saṅkhāra disappears.

132
00:11:53,934 --> 00:11:54,735
[SPEAKER_01]: It's other way around.

133
00:11:55,735 --> 00:11:59,257
[SPEAKER_01]: It's by subduing, fully purifying, fully developing

134
00:12:00,772 --> 00:12:08,814
[SPEAKER_01]: Samādhi, on account of a joy, on account of a non-speaking mouth that hasn't been engaging in careless speech, you quiet your thoughts.

135
00:12:08,854 --> 00:12:13,495
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you quiet the speaking mouth and your thoughts will quiet down.

136
00:12:13,875 --> 00:12:19,937
[SPEAKER_01]: Because each time you speak carelessly, your thoughts spill through speech into that world and maintain your wrong views about it.

137
00:12:21,357 --> 00:12:22,458
[SPEAKER_01]: So, you want to quiet your thoughts?

138
00:12:22,918 --> 00:12:23,618
[SPEAKER_01]: Quiet your speech.

139
00:12:24,218 --> 00:12:27,079
[SPEAKER_01]: And it will take it as long as it took you to quiet down your virtue.

140
00:12:28,578 --> 00:12:30,819
[SPEAKER_01]: Depending on the type of effort and quality you invested.

141
00:12:31,659 --> 00:12:43,563
[SPEAKER_01]: You know, somebody who is immoral, not virtuous, starts keeping the precepts, it's going to be a bit hard in the beginning, and they wouldn't see any aggregate of virtue there, doing it, keeping the precepts for them, and like, you know, they would have to do it.

142
00:12:44,044 --> 00:12:52,627
[SPEAKER_01]: But if you sustain it, keeping the precepts becomes effortless, because it never was about doing certain things, it was simply about abstaining from doing certain things.

143
00:12:53,388 --> 00:12:57,529
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's when that precept, sīla, starts keeping you, so to speak.

144
00:12:58,270 --> 00:12:58,730
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, same.

145
00:12:59,150 --> 00:13:05,252
[SPEAKER_01]: Abstain from spilling out into the world through your mouth, through careless pressure, through awkwardness, through any other unwholesome states, through doubt.

146
00:13:05,932 --> 00:13:08,733
[SPEAKER_01]: And your silence will keep your mind composed.

147
00:13:09,113 --> 00:13:09,473
[SPEAKER_01]: That's it.

148
00:13:11,809 --> 00:13:13,991
[SPEAKER_01]: So, still in the speech, quiet is the thoughts.

149
00:13:14,211 --> 00:13:17,955
[SPEAKER_01]: Then, when the thoughts are even quieted further in the second jhāna, that's the complete silence.

150
00:13:18,355 --> 00:13:22,880
[SPEAKER_01]: But you don't have to worry about the second jhāna until you have developed... until you've developed the first jhāna.

151
00:13:23,220 --> 00:13:26,824
[SPEAKER_01]: And you shouldn't worry about the first jhāna until you've developed your virtue and your speech beforehand.

152
00:13:28,285 --> 00:13:32,850
[SPEAKER_01]: But it is... it is like the first... the speech ceases in the first jhāna.

153
00:13:33,898 --> 00:13:43,430
[SPEAKER_01]: Not because you entered the magical state of your thought, but because you got so imperturbed, so established in an existence of a non-speaking mouth that has been enduring for a while.

154
00:13:44,271 --> 00:13:50,619
[SPEAKER_01]: And even when it spoke, it spoke on account of things that were practical or connected with dhamma and nothing else.

155
00:13:52,383 --> 00:13:56,344
[SPEAKER_01]: So, that's another reason why solitude is necessary for that type of development.

156
00:13:56,825 --> 00:14:05,528
[SPEAKER_01]: You can't be in the world where people constantly try to communicate and talk to you and expect to sustain that level of non-speaking existence.

157
00:14:07,909 --> 00:14:19,933
[SPEAKER_01]: But you can certainly purify a great deal of all the perversions in regard to your views about what comes first in the world, even in the world, even in, you know, in day-to-day life.

158
00:14:21,216 --> 00:14:23,877
[SPEAKER_01]: Just be mindful of, literally, of your mouth.

159
00:14:24,658 --> 00:14:27,639
[SPEAKER_01]: Be mindful of what comes out of it, what you're saying, why you're saying it.

160
00:14:28,220 --> 00:14:28,760
[SPEAKER_01]: Don't just...

161
00:14:28,780 --> 00:14:32,081
[SPEAKER_01]: I'll just say it and then fully give in to what you... No.

162
00:14:32,442 --> 00:14:36,904
[SPEAKER_01]: Okay, I'll say it and I'll remain mindful while I'm saying it and I'll remain mindful after I said it.

163
00:14:38,044 --> 00:14:41,426
[SPEAKER_01]: Because usually it's I'm mindful, I'm mindful, as in I'm refusing to say it.

164
00:14:42,367 --> 00:14:43,187
[SPEAKER_01]: Then I can't help it.

165
00:14:43,267 --> 00:14:46,269
[SPEAKER_01]: Then I decide to say it and mindfulness disappears and I say it.

166
00:14:46,629 --> 00:14:47,529
[SPEAKER_01]: That doesn't need to happen.

167
00:14:47,589 --> 00:14:48,850
[SPEAKER_01]: You can remain mindful throughout.

168
00:14:50,301 --> 00:14:53,023
[SPEAKER_01]: Even before you decide to say it, you should be mindful.

169
00:14:53,203 --> 00:14:54,884
[SPEAKER_01]: If you decide to say it, you should be mindful.

170
00:14:55,125 --> 00:14:56,526
[SPEAKER_01]: After you said it, you should be mindful.

171
00:14:59,668 --> 00:15:05,412
[SPEAKER_01]: Which then means, the reasons for you saying it in the first place will be clearer and clearer and clearer.

172
00:15:06,052 --> 00:15:07,754
[SPEAKER_01]: So, yeah, practice silence.

173
00:15:09,615 --> 00:15:13,538
[SPEAKER_01]: As I said, not as a kind of sense of external duty or some observance.

174
00:15:14,592 --> 00:15:22,858
[SPEAKER_01]: But there's a sense of, no, no, no, this is the gateway, one of the gateways, the mouth, one of the domains of action, body, speech and mind.

175
00:15:24,939 --> 00:15:27,581
[SPEAKER_01]: And it will develop your samādhi as well.

176
00:15:27,621 --> 00:15:40,570
[SPEAKER_01]: Obviously, there will be no practice of right speech and silence and non-speaking mouth, as I like to say, if your physical behavior has not already been honed and tamed to a great deal.

177
00:15:41,911 --> 00:15:44,273
[SPEAKER_01]: So, gradual training.

